  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Suppose the array has n elements, if 1 through n are all present.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4540,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 136,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "The answer is n plus 1.",
      "start_ms": 5180,
      "end_ms": 7180,
      "start_frame": 155,
      "end_frame": 215,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "Otherwise, at least one number between 1 and n is missing.",
      "start_ms": 7640,
      "end_ms": 11920,
      "start_frame": 229,
      "end_frame": 358,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "So the first missing positive must be between 1 and n plus 1.",
      "start_ms": 12700,
      "end_ms": 17200,
      "start_frame": 381,
      "end_frame": 516,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "That means we only need to arrange values from 1 through n.",
      "start_ms": 17760,
      "end_ms": 21780,
      "start_frame": 533,
      "end_frame": 653,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "Here is the rule.",
      "start_ms": 22140,
      "end_ms": 23040,
      "start_frame": 664,
      "end_frame": 691,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "Value x belongs at index x minus 1.",
      "start_ms": 23360,
      "end_ms": 26960,
      "start_frame": 701,
      "end_frame": 809,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "Why?",
      "start_ms": 27380,
      "end_ms": 27780,
      "start_frame": 821,
      "end_frame": 833,
      "word_count": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Because index 0 can represent 1, index 1 can represent 2, and so on.",
      "start_ms": 27780,
      "end_ms": 34540,
      "start_frame": 833,
      "end_frame": 1036,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "The array becomes its own presence map.",
      "start_ms": 35080,
      "end_ms": 37560,
      "start_frame": 1052,
      "end_frame": 1127,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "At each position, while a current number is in that valid range, move it into its home by swapping.",
      "start_ms": 38160,
      "end_ms": 45020,
      "start_frame": 1145,
      "end_frame": 1351,
      "word_count": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "After a swap, check the new value at the same position.",
      "start_ms": 45680,
      "end_ms": 49680,
      "start_frame": 1370,
      "end_frame": 1490,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "It may need a different home.",
      "start_ms": 50420,
      "end_ms": 52500,
      "start_frame": 1513,
      "end_frame": 1575,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "But if the destination already holds the same number, stop.",
      "start_ms": 52980,
      "end_ms": 57280,
      "start_frame": 1589,
      "end_frame": 1718,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Otherwise duplicates could keep us swapping forever.",
      "start_ms": 57280,
      "end_ms": 61100,
      "start_frame": 1718,
      "end_frame": 1833,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Negative values, 0 and values larger than n have no useful home here.",
      "start_ms": 61720,
      "end_ms": 67780,
      "start_frame": 1852,
      "end_frame": 2033,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "So skip them.",
      "start_ms": 68500,
      "end_ms": 69480,
      "start_frame": 2055,
      "end_frame": 2084,
      "word_count": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "Once placement is complete, scan from the left.",
      "start_ms": 70060,
      "end_ms": 73000,
      "start_frame": 2102,
      "end_frame": 2190,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "The first position that does not hold index plus 1 tells us the smallest missing positive.",
      "start_ms": 73780,
      "end_ms": 79940,
      "start_frame": 2213,
      "end_frame": 2398,
      "word_count": 16
    },
    {
      "text": "Let's trace the actual swaps.",
      "start_ms": 80800,
      "end_ms": 82980,
      "start_frame": 2424,
      "end_frame": 2489,
      "word_count": 5
    }
  ],
